Prior art
================================================================================

None of the projects below contributed code to this one. They are credited because
they solved a neighbouring problem first, and reading them shaped what mcstage does
and does not try to do. Stars, licences and last-push dates were checked on
2026-08-25.

  jpenilla/run-task              Apache-2.0   Boots a real Paper, Folia or Velocity
                                 363 stars    from Gradle, and does it well. The
                                              closest existing thing to this, and
                                              the reason mcstage is a CLI: run-task
                                              belongs to one build tool.
  MockBukkit/MockBukkit          MIT          A mock server to assert against. The
                                 742 stars    other half of the problem: it never
                                              starts a server, so the failures it
                                              cannot have are the ones here.
  headlesshq/mc-runtime-test     MIT          Boots the game in CI, on the client
                                 61 stars     side, headless. Same idea aimed at the
                                              other end of the connection.
  itzg/docker-minecraft-server   Apache-2.0   The way most people run a server in a
                                 14193 stars  container, and the reference for what
                                              a server directory should look like.
                                              Aimed at operating a server rather
                                              than at changing plugin code.
  Tiiffi/mcrcon                  Zlib         Driving a server console over RCON.
                                 1075 stars   mcstage uses the process's own stdin
                                              instead, so there is no port to open
                                              and no password to invent, but mcrcon
                                              is why the alternative was understood
                                              before being ruled out.
  Minecrell/TerminalConsoleAppender
                                 MIT          The console layer Paper actually uses,
                                 81 stars     and the reason piped input works.
  Minecrell/SimpleTerminalConsole
                                 no licence   Its companion, read for the same
                                              reason. Nothing is copied from it.
  jline/jline3                   NOASSERTION  The terminal library underneath, read
                                 1796 stars   to establish when a system terminal is
                                              attempted at all.
  PaperMC/Paper                  mixed        The server nearly everything here runs.
                                 12599 stars  GitHub reports NOASSERTION: the API and
                                              the server are not under one licence.
  PaperMC/Folia                  GPL-3.0      Regionised threading, and the second
                                 4335 stars   platform this boots.
  PurpurMC/Purpur                MIT          The third, and a second build API with
                                 2397 stars   different habits, which is how the
                                              digest handling stopped being specific
                                              to one publisher.

  SalyyS1/foliascan              Apache-2.0   Earlier tool by the same author: where
                                              a plugin jar breaks on Folia.
  SalyyS1/pluginscope             Apache-2.0  Earlier tool by the same author: what is
                                              inside a plugin jar and what it targets.
                                              Its console reporter and CLI shape are
                                              followed here.
  SalyyS1/serverdoctor            Apache-2.0  Earlier tool by the same author: reading
                                              a server that has already run. mcstage is
                                              the other direction — it produces the log
                                              rather than reading one — and the
